Thanks so much, Karl!

One quick follow-up: how did you determine that that last marker (SLCL|SCAFFOLD_8_47238483) was unlinked to the rest of the chromosome?

While there is still some dip in the LOD profile, now most of chromosome 8 is continuously above the LOD threshold, with a 37 Mb C.I. according to `bayesint`.  There’s also no evidence for 2 QTL versus 1 QTL, based on `scantwo`:

```
summary(x2)
      pos1f pos2f lod.full lod.fv1 lod.int <http://lod.int>     pos1a pos2a lod.add lod.av1
c8:c8  10.0  31.0     9.12    3.12   1.585      31.0  61.0    7.54   1.534
```

Given permutation results:
```
DR (1000 permutations)
    full  fv1  int  add  av1  one
5%  9.60 7.54 6.26 6.42 4.17 3.64
10% 9.08 7.13 5.80 5.96 3.86 3.26
```

So, I suppose this is one more case study of how bi-parental crosses often do not given very refined QTL positions in the F2 generation.

Thanks again for taking a look!

Best,
Scott

